{"name":"Champagne","hex":"#e9d2ac","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Champagne","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A cultural region and former province of France, the terroir of the wine champagne; now part of Grand Est region.","A surname from French."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of champagne (“type of sparkling wine made in France”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Champagne"}],"entries":[{"title":"Champagne","blocks":[{"text":"Champagne is a sparkling wine originated and produced in the Champagne wine region of France under the AOC rules of the appellation, which demand specific vineyard practices, sourcing of grapes exclusively from designated places within it, specific grape-pressing methods and secondary fermentation of the wine in the bottle to cause carbonation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Glass_of_champagne.jpg/330px-Glass_of_champagne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Champagne"},{"title":"Champagne (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color champagne is a name given for various very pale tints of yellowish-orange that are close to beige. The color's name is derived from the typical color of the beverage Champagne."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3e/Quartz-Topaz-gem7-76d.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Champagne_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/A_village_with_vineyards_in_Champagne%2C_France_1987.jpg/500px-A_village_with_vineyards_in_Champagne%2C_France_1987.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/A_village_with_vineyards_in_Champagne%2C_France_1987.jpg/1280px-A_village_with_vineyards_in_Champagne%2C_Fr